    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n53330" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κᾰρηκομόωντες</span></b> , οἱ,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κομάω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>with hair on the head, long-haired</i>, epith. of the
			Achaians, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				2.11
			</span></i>, al. (sed divisim scrib.): Com. metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐχῖνοι κ. ἀκάνθαις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Matro
					<u>Conv.</u>
					18
				</span></i>
			:—hence Verb <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καρηκομόω</span></b> , coined by <i><span class="en">
				Diog.
				<u>Ep.</u>
				19
			</span></i>.</div>
